Heartfelt by Martijn Steinrucken aka BigWings (2017)
Shadertoy: https://www.shadertoy.com/view/ltffzl

Source of this port: Heartfelt.frag in the KDE Shader Wallpaper project,
https://raw.githubusercontent.com/y4my4my4m/kde-shader-wallpaper/HEAD/package/contents/ui/Shaders/Heartfelt.frag
(commit f9eed3d2f6d73f0a5c7e20ef00072be062f1d4bf of
https://github.com/y4my4my4m/kde-shader-wallpaper). That project is GPL-3.0, but
this shader is not covered by that: the shader carries its own licence in its
own header, quoted below, and this port follows that licence.

The author's notice, line 3 of the header of Heartfelt.frag at the address above,
reads, word for word:

  // License Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 3.0 Unported License.

Ported to Metal Shading Language for MacOS Live Wallpaper; see the note at the
top of main.metal for what was changed. In short:

  - The image the original refracts through the raindrops (a photo supplied by
    the host) is not shipped. It is replaced by LwNight() in main.metal, a soft
    procedural picture of blurred night-city lights. That picture is ADDED BY THE
    PORT; it is not part of the original and is not the author's work.
  - Mouse input removed; time runs at 60% of real time and starts 10 seconds into
    the author's 102-second story. The author faded the picture to black at each
    end of the story; here the picture is not faded, and for the first 6 seconds
    of each story the end of the one before dissolves into it. The lightning
    flash is a gentle glow instead of a flicker; a few lines were rewritten for Metal (smoothstep with reversed
    edges, a vignette expression with an unordered side effect, the output
    parameter).
  - The author's algorithm, constants and look are otherwise unchanged.

A note on one credit inside the author's code. The hash function N13() is
marked in the author's own comment as "from DAVE HOSKINS" (his "Hash without
Sine"). It is a few lines of arithmetic and is kept exactly as the author wrote
it. A copy of Dave Hoskins' own shader source found in a third-party archive
(github.com/tmsampson/enginejs, shader_joy/resources/shadertoy-downloader/
shaders/Dave_Hoskins/Hash without Sine.fs) carries the header "Creative Commons
Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International Public License. Created by David
Hoskins." That is a different licence from the one on this shader, and it could
not be checked against the Shadertoy page itself, which does not allow automated
access, nor against the version that existed when Heartfelt was written in 2017.
Anyone who needs the scene to contain no code from that source can replace N13()
with a hash of their own; the look stays the same, with a different random
arrangement of drops.

This port is an adaptation of the original shader and is offered under the same
licence, Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 3.0 Unported. It
may not be used commercially.

